WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.091 --> 00:00:14.804
<v Maya>You know, it used to be that global security had this very comforting, almost architectural logic to it. Right. Like if a bank vault gets blown open with military grade explosives, you know, it wasn't just a</v>

2
00:00:14.864 --> 00:00:17.266
<v Maya>couple of teenagers with a crowbar, you know.</v>

3
00:00:17.747 --> 00:00:18.267
<v Daniel>Exactly.</v>

4
00:00:18.327 --> 00:00:25.714
<v Maya>For decades, there was this direct correlation between the complexity of an event and the actual resources of the people who pulled it off.</v>

5
00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:40.977
<v Daniel>And in the digital world, I mean, we call this attribution, it basically acted as this incredibly reliable sorting mechanism for us. If an intelligence operation or a cyber attack was highly sophisticated, say, it used custom malware or</v>

6
