20
00:01:53.553 --> 00:02:08.324
<v Daniel>And to do that, we have to look at the central claim of this anthropic report. The core thesis here is that AI has entirely collapsed the labor and tooling gap that used to separate well-resourced state operations from lone individuals. The report states this directly for threat</v>

21
00:02:08.344 --> 00:02:16.190
<v Daniel>intelligence investigators. And it says sophistication has stopped being a reliable signal of who is behind an operation.</v>

22
00:02:16.593 --> 00:02:20.135
<v Maya>I mean, that single sentence is the spine of our entire conversation today.</v>

23
00:02:20.155 --> 00:02:20.995
<v Daniel>Yeah, it really is.</v>

24
00:02:21.295 --> 00:02:32.521
<v Maya>Sophistication has stopped being a reliable signal. OK, let's just unpack this, because to understand how this gap collapsed so incredibly quickly, we have to look at exactly what changed in just one year.</v>

25
00:02:32.541 --> 00:02:45.688
<v Daniel>Right. The timeline here is critical, because if we look back at Anthropic's threat report from August 2025, which is just a little over a year ago. Threat actors were using AI mostly for what we would basically call assistance.</v>

26
00:02:45.908 --> 00:02:46.929
<v Maya>Like a digital helper.</v>

27
00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:52.415
<v Daniel>Exactly. It could, you know, draft a phishing email or maybe help debug a simple script.</v>

28
00:02:52.595 --> 00:02:55.358
<v Maya>So it was just a tool, like you still had to swing the hammer yourself.</v>

29
00:02:55.458 --> 00:03:05.488
<v Daniel>Yes. But the paradigm in this new September 2026 report has completely shifted to automation. The report describes AI actually running the cyber kill chain.</v>

30
00:03:05.727 --> 00:03:20.539
