156
00:17:40.162 --> 00:17:48.568
<v Maya>Because right now we really have to ask, is voluntary vendor reporting just the floor of what we should expect? Or is it becoming the ceiling of what the public ever gets to know?</v>

157
00:17:48.929 --> 00:17:51.130
<v Daniel>That is the critical governance question right now.</v>

158
00:17:51.571 --> 00:18:01.138
<v Maya>So what does this mean when you're scrolling through the news tomorrow? For you, the everyday person who isn't a cybersecurity professional, how does this change the way we understand the world?</v>

159
00:18:01.755 --> 00:18:04.316
<v Daniel>Well, it basically means the death of attribution as we knew it.</v>

160
00:18:04.436 --> 00:18:04.636
<v Maya>Yeah.</v>

161
00:18:05.037 --> 00:18:19.764
<v Daniel>If you read a headline tomorrow about a highly sophisticated cyber attack, one that compromised thousands of systems and moved laterally across networks with incredible precision, you can no longer assume it was gated by immense expertise and</v>

162
00:18:19.824 --> 00:18:34.734
<v Daniel>expense. Right. The assumption that dangerous work stays expensive is just gone. It might have been a nation state. But it also might have been a small, financially motivated crew who bought some stolen credentials and spun up a fleet of AI agents to do the work of 50</v>

163
00:18:34.794 --> 00:18:35.275
<v Daniel>engineers.</v>

164
00:18:35.535 --> 00:18:39.458
<v Maya>The labor gap is gone. The intent is what matters now, not the sophistication.</v>

165
00:18:39.678 --> 00:18:40.139
<v Daniel>Exactly.</v>

166
00:18:40.279 --> 00:18:49.967
<v Maya>I want to leave you with a final thought to really mull over. We started today by talking about how a blown vault used to mean military-grade explosives and expert thieves.</v>

167
00:18:50.007 --> 00:18:50.928
<v Daniel>Yeah, the old logic.</v>

168
00:18:51.228 --> 00:19:06.039
<v Maya>But now the tools to crack the digital vault are practically free and infinitely reproducible. The next time a massive cyber incident hits the news and you see a Lourdes quickly pointing the finger at a specific nation state based purely on the sophistication of the</v>

169
00:19:06.079 --> 00:19:07.700
<v Maya>code, ask yourself this</v>

170
00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:08.180
<v Daniel>race.</v>

171
00:19:08.681 --> 00:19:20.489
<v Maya>How will global politics adapt? How will diplomacy even function when governments can no longer easily prove if they were attacked by a hostile superpower or just a single person sitting in a basement with an API key?</v>

172
00:19:20.724 --> 00:19:24.002
<v Daniel>The entire architecture of deterrence has to be rebuilt from the ground up.</v>

173
00:19:24.123 --> 00:19:24.791
<v Maya>It really does.</v>
